@startuml
title PayLink - Failed Payment Release and Completed-Payment Refund Request
autonumber
actor Customer
actor "Support Employee" as Support
participant "PayLink API" as API
participant "Payment / Refund Service" as Service
participant "Wallet / Ledger" as Wallet
participant "Payment Event / Audit" as Audit
participant "Notification Service" as Notify

== Automatic release after a failed bill payment ==
Service -> Wallet: release held funds (HOLD_RELEASE)
Wallet --> Service: funds returned to available balance
Service -> Audit: record ledger movement and audit record
Service -> Service: Payment Failed -> Refunded
Service -> Audit: record PaymentEvent
Service -> Notify: send failure SMS

note over Service,Wallet
This flow applies when the biller confirms failure.
An Unknown payment is NOT refunded automatically.
Its funds remain held until a later callback
or reconciliation establishes the outcome.
end note

== Customer requests refund for a Completed payment ==
Customer -> API: request refund(payment reference, reason)
API -> Service: create refund request
Service -> Service: verify payment is Completed
Service -> Service: create Refund(status=Pending)
Service -> Audit: audit refund request
Service -> Notify: notify support
Service --> API: pending refund reference
API --> Customer: request received

Support -> API: approve or reject refund
API -> Service: review pending refund
alt Approved
  Service -> Wallet: create REFUND ledger entry\nfor approved amount
  Wallet --> Service: refund credited
  Service -> Audit: audit money movement and approval
  Service -> Service: Refund.status = Approved
  note right of Service
    Original Payment remains Completed.
    Refund is a separate record and does
    not change the Payment state.
  end note
  Service -> Notify: notify customer of approval
  Service --> API: approved
else Rejected
  Service -> Service: Refund.status = Rejected
  Service -> Audit: audit rejection and reason
  Service -> Notify: notify customer of rejection
  Service --> API: rejected; no money moved
end
API --> Customer: refund decision
@enduml
